efw_alert.body:
Source: {source}
ID: {object_id}
Amount: {amount} {currency}
Customer: {customer_ref}
Dashboard: {dashboard_url}

The card issuer has flagged this payment as suspected fraud (early fraud warning).
Consider issuing a proactive refund before it turns into a chargeback. If the order has not shipped, hold the shipment.
No action is needed if you have already refunded it or confirmed the transaction is legitimate.

deadline_reminder.body:
Source: {source}
ID: {object_id}
Amount: {amount} {currency}
Customer: {customer_ref}
Evidence due by: {evidence_due_by_jst} (JST, exact time)
Days left: {days_left}
Dashboard: {dashboard_url}

If no evidence is submitted by the deadline, the dispute is lost automatically. Aim to submit at least 24 hours before the deadline.

refund_failed.body:
Source: {source}
ID: {object_id}
Amount: {amount} {currency}
Customer: {customer_ref}
Failure reason: {failure_reason}
Dashboard: {dashboard_url}

The customer has not been refunded. Check the reason in the dashboard, then retry or refund by another method (e.g. bank transfer).

cb_rate_alert.body:
Month: {month}
Disputes: {disputes}
Successful payments: {payments}
Chargeback rate: {rate}% (threshold {threshold}%, level {level})

Each card network defines the numerator, denominator and thresholds differently. The values in this template are a guide only; check each network's current program rules.

error_notice.body:
Workflow: {workflow_name}
Failed node: {last_node}
Error: {message}
Execution log: {execution_url}

Check the execution log for the cause, fix it, and re-run. Sheet writes or emails may have partially completed, so check the ledger sheet before re-running.
